{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The words of the preacher, the son of David, king of Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Vanity of vanities, saith the preacher, vanity of vanities; all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What profit hath a man of all his labor, which he taketh under the sun?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " generation passeth away, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "another",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " generation cometh: but the earth abideth for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sun also riseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he arose.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wind goeth towards the south, and turneth about to the north; it whirleth about continually, and the wind returneth again according to its circuits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not full; to the place from whence the rivers come, thither they return again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " full of labor; man cannot utter ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The thing that hath been, it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which shall be; and that which is done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that which shall be done: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no new ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is there ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thing of which it may be said, See, this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " new? it hath been already of old time, which was before us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no remembrance of former ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; neither shall there be ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " remembrance of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that are to come with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "those",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that shall come after.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I the preacher was king over Israel in Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I gave my heart to seek and search out by wisdom concerning all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that are done under heaven: this grievous labor hath God given to the sons of man to be exercised with it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and behold, all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity and vexation of spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " crooked cannot be made straight: and that which is wanting cannot be numbered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I communed with my own heart, saying, Lo, I have come to great estate, and have gained more wisdom than all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that have been before me in Jerusalem: and my heart had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I gave my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly: I perceived that this also is vexation of spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.1.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.1.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in much wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " much grief: and he that increaseth knowledge increaseth sorrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
